{
 "encounter_id": "00978",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Mr Gilligan, thanks for coming. The booking says a review of your tablets, because of the nosebleeds."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's right. My wife says I'm to ask. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's go through your tablets, one by one."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Apixaban, 5 mg, twice a day. Bisoprolol, 5 mg, once a day. Ramipril, 5 mg, once a day. Atorvastatin, 40 mg, at night. And omeprazole, 20 mg, in the morning."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good, you know them well. Do you ever miss the apixaban? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Never. It's on the kitchen table, in front of the kettle. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's an excellent system. Any health conditions that go with them?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The heart rhythm thing, atrial fibrillation. And high blood pressure."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check you. Pulse 64, blood pressure 130 over 76, temperature 36.6, oxygen 98 percent, breathing 14, weight 85 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Good numbers? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Very good. Pulse is a nice slow one on the bisoprolol. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's the idea. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any dizzy spells, Mr Gilligan?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, no dizziness at all."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Now, here's how I think about it. The apixaban thins the blood, which protects you from a stroke from the heart rhythm, but it makes bleeding from the nose more likely. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So it's the tablet? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's a contributor. But the benefit of the apixaban is large. I wouldn't want to stop it for nosebleeds alone. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's what the other doctor said. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good, we agree. The better approach is to make the nose less likely to bleed. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "How do I do that? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Keep the inside of the nose moist. A small amount of petroleum jelly, just inside each nostril, twice a day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Vaseline. I have that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A saline spray works as well. And avoid picking and forceful nose blowing."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My wife says I'm a picker. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "She's observant. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "She is. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "When a nosebleed does come, sit up, lean forward, pinch the soft part of your nose for ten minutes, and breathe through your mouth."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ten minutes, by the clock. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And don't lean back, because the blood runs down your throat. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Humidity helps too. A bowl of water by the radiator at night. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Good idea. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If a nosebleed lasts more than twenty minutes, go straight to the emergency department."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will do. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And ring us if they're happening more than twice a week. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Understood. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
